urrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-30401da41c4e4e69a7d75d54ac811e73","line":24,"path":"rules/migrations.blade.php","start_column":43}],"path":"rules/migrations.blade.php","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"EA2","severity":"MEDIUM","start_column":43,"tags":["Excessive Agency"]},{"category":"Output Handling","code_snippet":"\n## Throttle high-volume exception reports\n\nA failing integration can flood logs or error tracking. Configure `throttle()` with a `Lottery` or `Limit` result to sample or rate-limit matching exception reports. Choose keys deliberately when separate exception classes, tenants, or integrations need independent limits.\n\n## Prevent duplicate reports of one exception instance\n","confidence":0.8,"evidence":{},"finding":"flood log","finding_ids":["finding-4b5edd26b02b456aa865a28dab36efbc"],"id":"sha256:349111dd7f514627aaba0777c2081b1a94d48594530edde010c7c971246cd980","intent":null,"line":49,"match_fingerprint":"20b945c1b12b44f7e0991d81616241a739dacb42702f26db27d925baec0e691b","message":"Output size or generation rate is not bounded. Unbounded output enables denial-of-service through resource exhaustion, log flooding, or context-window stuffing.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-4b5edd26b02b456aa865a28dab36efbc","line":49,"path":"rules/error-handling.md","start_column":26}],"path":"rules/error-handling.md","pattern":"Unbounded Output","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Set explicit limits on output length, generation count, and rate. Use max_tokens and truncation to prevent unbounded output.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"OH3","severity":"MEDIUM","start_column":26,"tags":["Output Handling"]},{"category":"Excessive Agency","code_snippet":"\n## Use `ShouldDispatchAfterCommit` inside transactions\n\nWhen you dispatch an event inside a database transaction, `ShouldDispatchAfterCommit` delays dispatch until all open database transactions commit. If a transaction rolls back, Laravel discards the event. The delay affects synchronous and queued listeners. It is not limited to queue timing.\n\n```php\nclass OrderShipped implements ShouldDispatchAfterCommit {}","confidence":0.7,"evidence":{},"finding":"not limited to","finding_ids":["finding-03b385d140a9404b8eb11f22dda55c51"],"id":"sha256:964580e1e90c2f3c5e70d7fe2fbfcc918140fd9fa02b0c3b4fa101830df6d663","intent":null,"line":16,"match_fingerprint":"943d9aae8743c129fe98eb6cc5e984f5e35ceba0b44ce4ca00f42b97f0bf3eaf","message":"Skill's behavior or capabilities extend beyond its stated purpose. Scope creep allows an agent to perform actions unrelated to its documented functionality, increasing the attack surface.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-03b385d140a9404b8eb11f22dda55c51","line":16,"path":"rules/events-notifications.blade.php","start_column":262}],"path":"rules/events-notifications.blade.php","pattern":"Scope Creep","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Limit the skill's scope to its documented purpose. Remove instructions that enable the agent to perform actions outside its stated functionality.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"EA3","severity":"LOW","start_column":262,"tags":["Excessive Agency"]}],"findings_truncated":false,"freshness":"current","id":"laravel/boost/laravel-best-practices","kind":"standalone_skill","plugin_path":null,"profile":{"digest":"sha256:a73e7c4a9fa0ac563a885c541d207e90dde2e248ca426f7824cf429d725db921","id":"static-standard-v3"},"raw_finding_count":15,"report_digest":"sha256:7a0bdf9b5f8d326a3d5397e63312fd4c661bd2a33fc921402af9b7b1ceef4068","retry":{"attempt_count":1,"disposition":"blocked","latest_status":"partial","next_attempt_at":null,"next_profile":null,"reason":"reference_missing"},"scanned_at":"2026-10-30T16:01:25Z","scanner":{"id":"skillspector","revision":"f3b25697d76256998ca9d42c198d256258d